    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jmoneco.2026.103956",
      "sequence": 2,
      "source_sequence": 2,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Unconventional monetary policy spillovers and the (in)convenience of Treasuries",
      "title_cn": "非常规货币政策的溢出效应和国债的便利性",
      "authors": [
        "Karlye Dilts Stedman",
        "Andrew Hanson"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Foreign monetary policy shocks increasingly influence U.S. yields, particularly since the Global Financial Crisis. We show that this heightened sensitivity reflects both the adoption of unconventional monetary policy tools and a decline in the convenience of Treasuries. Using high frequency identification, we find that when Treasuries command a low convenience premium—behaving more like other assets—they respond more to ECB monetary policy, consistent with increased sensitivity to portfolio rebalancing. A two-country preferred-habitat model with time-varying covariance of yields rationalizes these results: when Treasuries are less convenient, they become closer substitutes for foreign equivalents, amplifying cross-border transmission of policy shocks.",
      "abstract_cn": "外国货币政策冲击对美国收益率的影响越来越大，特别是自全球金融危机以来。我们表明，这种敏感性的提高既反映了非常规货币政策工具的采用，也反映了国债便利性的下降。通过高频识别，我们发现，当国债具有较低的便利溢价（表现得更像其他资产）时，它们对欧洲央行货币政策的反应更大，这与对投资组合再平衡的敏感性增加一致。具有随时间变化的收益率协方差的二国家首选栖息地模型使这些结果合理化：当国债不太方便时，它们成为外国同类货币更接近的替代品，从而放大政策冲击的跨境传导。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jmoneco.2026.103956",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304393226000711?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
