    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jmoneco.2026.103961",
      "sequence": 3,
      "source_sequence": 3,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Evaluating macroeconomic outcomes under asymmetries: Expectations matter",
      "title_cn": "评估不对称情况下的宏观经济结果：预期很重要",
      "authors": [
        "Brent Bundick",
        "Isabel Cairó",
        "Nicolas Petrosky-Nadeau"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Asymmetries play an important role in many macroeconomic models. We show that assumptions on household and firm expectations play a key role in determining the effects of these asymmetries on macroeconomic outcomes. If households and firms have perfect foresight and hence do not account for the possibility of future shocks, then the implied longer-run averages and distributions can differ significantly from their rational expectations counterparts. We first derive this result analytically in a standard New Keynesian environment under either an asymmetric monetary policy rule or a nonlinear Phillips curve before numerically examining some of the key nonlinearities featured in the recent literature.",
      "abstract_cn": "不对称性在许多宏观经济模型中发挥着重要作用。我们表明，对家庭和企业预期的假设在确定这些不对称性对宏观经济结果的影响方面发挥着关键作用。如果家庭和企业具有完美的远见，因此没有考虑未来冲击的可能性，那么隐含的长期平均值和分布可能与其理性预期有很大不同。我们第一在标准新凯恩斯主义环境下，在不对称货币政策规则或非线性菲利普斯曲线下分析得出这一结果，然后对最近文献中的一些关键非线性进行数值研究。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jmoneco.2026.103961",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304393226000760?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
