    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jmoneco.2026.103959",
      "sequence": 4,
      "source_sequence": 4,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Central bank communication by ??? The economics of monetary policy leaks",
      "title_cn": "央行沟通方式？？？货币政策的经济学泄漏",
      "authors": [
        "Michael Ehrmann",
        "Phillipp Gnan",
        "Kilian Rieder"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Using a novel database of media-reported anonymous leaks about monetary policy in the euro area, we conduct the first systematic empirical analysis of these confidential information disclosures originating from central banks. Our database reveals that Eurosystem leaks are frequent – in particular relative to leaks from other major central banks. We provide evidence that many Eurosystem leaks are likely not accidents, but placed strategically by insiders. Exploiting high-frequency financial market reactions to leaks, we find that they have large effects on markets relative to standard monetary surprises, often exceeding the impact of attributed statements by policy-makers. Yet, mainly reflecting minority opinions, leaks do not usually lock in decision-making. Post-meeting leaks regularly reveal information about dissent on the committee, changing market perceptions about the strength of the policy signal. Post-meeting leaks thereby reverse some of the initial market effect of official policy announcements.",
      "abstract_cn": "利用媒体报道的有关欧元区货币政策的匿名泄密事件的新颖数据库，我们对这些来自中央银行的机密信息披露进行了系统的实证分析。我们的数据库显示，欧元体系的泄密事件很频繁——特别是相对于其他主要央行的泄密事件。我们提供的证据表明，许多欧元体系泄密事件可能并非意外，而是内部人士的战略性安排。利用金融市场对泄密事件的高频反应，我们发现，相对于标准的货币意外事件，它们对市场的影响很大，往往超过了政策制定者声明的影响。然而，泄密主要反映少数人的意见，通常不会锁定决策。会后泄密事件定期披露有关委员会异议的信息，改变了市场对政策信号强度的看法。因此，会后泄密的消息扭转了官方政策公告的一些最初市场效应。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jmoneco.2026.103959",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304393226000747?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
